  "goodToKnow": "Blechen is colloquial for paying, usually reluctantly or a lot: Für die Reparatur musste ich ordentlich blechen. Synonyms: berappen, löhnen. It comes from das Blech (sheet metal, tin), slang for coins. Das Blech is also colloquial for nonsense: Red kein Blech!, and der Blechschaden is minor bodywork damage after a crash. Die Blechtrommel (The Tin Drum) is Günter Grass's famous novel. Regular: blechte, geblecht."
